/// \class CastleBehavior
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_behavior_module_factories_a
/// \brief Behavior module registered as "CastleBehavior": an update and
///        create module configured by castle-unpack, crew, decal and
///        ownership fields; CastleUpgrade reaches it through an object's
///        CastleMemberBehavior.
///
/// This is one of the largest module classes in this group. Its
/// registered data factory is not documented in this group. The data's
/// parse step adds two tables. The first holds
/// \c RepairHealthPercentPerSecond (a percentage) and \c BuildVariation
/// (an integer). The second holds the castle fields:
/// \c CastleToUnpackForFaction, \c PreBuiltList,
/// \c PreBuiltPlyr, \c BuildTime, \c UnpackDelayTime, \c InstantUnpack,
/// \c ScanDistance, \c MaxCastleRadius, the crew fields (\c FilterCrew,
/// \c CrewPrepareTime, \c CrewPrepareInterval, \c CrewPrepareFX,
/// \c CrewReleaseFX), decal fields (\c FactionDecal, \c DecalName,
/// \c DecalSize), \c FadeTime (a real), \c FilterValidOwnedEntries,
/// \c KeepDeathKillsEverything, \c DisableStructureRotation,
/// \c EvaEnemyCastleSightedEvent, \c Summoned and
/// \c TransferFoundationHealthToCastleUponUnpack.
///
/// The names suggest, though this page does not confirm it, that this is
/// the main module of a castle or camp: the field names above and the
/// method names in the ledger (packing, unpacking and owned-object
/// registration among them) point to unpacking the castle into its
/// structures, packing it again and tracking the objects it owns. The
/// methods themselves are separate work and are not described here.
///
/// CastleUpgrade finds this module through CastleMemberBehavior: it reads
/// an object ID from the CastleMemberBehavior on its own object, looks that
/// object up and, if it still exists, finds this module on it by the
/// "CastleBehavior" name key and passes the upgrade to it (see
/// CastleUpgrade). BFME 1 already has the class.
///
/// \see CastleBehavior::friend_newModuleInstance, CastleMemberBehavior,
///      CastleUpgrade

/// \fn Module *CastleBehavior::friend_newModuleInstance(Thing *thing, const ModuleData *moduleData)
/// \brief Instance factory registered for "CastleBehavior": creates the
///        module for one object.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModule calls it through the registration. The group
/// page describes the shared frame; this one differs only in that the
/// class is too large for the short form of the size operand, which is
/// why its body is a few bytes longer than its neighbours'.
///
/// \param thing       The object being built; the module keeps it as its
///                    owner.
/// \param moduleData  The template's module data for this module line.
/// \return The new module as the Module base the factory stores, or null
///         when the allocation fails.
/// \see CastleBehavior


/// \class CastleMemberBehavior
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_behavior_module_factories_a
/// \brief Behavior module registered as "CastleMemberBehavior": refers its
///        object to a castle; CastleUpgrade uses it to find that castle.
///
/// CastleUpgrade looks this module up by name on its own object, reads the
/// ID of a castle object from it and, if that object still exists, passes
/// the upgrade to the castle object and to its CastleBehavior (see
/// CastleUpgrade). Its data class reads three EVA events whose names refer
/// to a destroyed camp, one each for the owner, allies and the
/// attacker (\c CampDestroyedOwnerEvaEvent, \c CampDestroyedAllyEvaEvent,
/// \c CampDestroyedAttackerEvaEvent), a sound (\c BeingBuiltSound) and two
/// booleans, \c StoreUpgradePrice and \c CountsForEvaCastleBreached.
/// Its registration carries only the bit Zero Hour uses for the damage
/// interface. BFME 1 already has the class.
///
/// \see CastleMemberBehavior::friend_newModuleInstance,
///      CastleMemberBehaviorModuleData::friend_newModuleData,
///      CastleBehavior

/// \class CastleMemberBehaviorModuleData
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_behavior_module_factories_a
/// \brief Module data for CastleMemberBehavior: camp EVA events, a sound
///        and two flags.
///
/// Built once per module line by
/// CastleMemberBehaviorModuleData::friend_newModuleData and shared by every
/// object of the template.

/// \fn Module *CastleMemberBehavior::friend_newModuleInstance(Thing *thing, const ModuleData *moduleData)
/// \brief Instance factory registered for "CastleMemberBehavior": creates
///        the module for one object.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModule calls it through the registration. The group
/// page describes the shared frame.
///
/// \param thing       The object being built; the module keeps it as its
///                    owner.
/// \param moduleData  The template's CastleMemberBehaviorModuleData.
/// \return The new module as the Module base the factory stores, or null
///         when the allocation fails.
/// \see CastleMemberBehaviorModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \fn ModuleData *CastleMemberBehaviorModuleData::friend_newModuleData(INI *ini)
/// \brief Data factory registered for "CastleMemberBehavior": creates the
///        module data and parses the module's INI block into it.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModuleDataFromINI calls it through the registration.
/// The group page describes the shared frame.
///
/// \param ini  The reader positioned on the module's block, or null to
///             keep the constructor defaults.
/// \return The new module data as the ModuleData base the factory stores.
/// \see CastleMemberBehavior::friend_newModuleInstance


/// \class ClearanceTestingSlowDeathBehavior
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_behavior_module_factories_a
/// \brief Slow-death module registered as "ClearanceTestingSlowDeathBehavior":
///        a slow death that also carries a clearance geometry and height
///        limits.
///
/// Its data class first takes SlowDeathBehaviorModuleData's two tables,
/// the slow-death fields and the death conditions (\c DeathTypes,
/// \c ExemptStatus, \c RequiredStatus, \c DamageAmountRequired,
/// \c MinKillerAngle, \c MaxKillerAngle; the group page lists both), and
/// then adds a clearance geometry (\c ClearanceGeometry,
/// \c ClearanceGeometryMajorRadius, \c ClearanceGeometryMinorRadius,
/// \c ClearanceGeometryRotationAnchorOffset, \c ClearanceGeometryHeight,
/// \c ClearanceGeometryIsSmall, \c ClearanceGeometryOffset) and four height
/// limits (\c ClearanceMaxHeight, \c ClearanceMaxHeightFraction,
/// \c ClearanceMinHeight, \c ClearanceMinHeightFraction). Most of the
/// geometry fields are read by GeometryInfo's parsers, such as
/// GeometryInfo::parseGeometryType, which Zero Hour also uses for an object
/// template's own \c Geometry fields. The name and fields
/// suggest that the death sequence tests the space around the object
/// against that geometry; this page does not describe the test. BFME 1
/// already has the class.
///
/// \see ClearanceTestingSlowDeathBehavior::friend_newModuleInstance,
///      ClearanceTestingSlowDeathBehaviorModuleData::friend_newModuleData,
///      GiantBirdSlowDeathBehavior

/// \class ClearanceTestingSlowDeathBehaviorModuleData
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_behavior_module_factories_a
/// \brief Module data for ClearanceTestingSlowDeathBehavior: the slow-death
///        and death-condition fields plus the clearance geometry and height
///        limits.
///
/// Built once per module line by
/// ClearanceTestingSlowDeathBehaviorModuleData::friend_newModuleData and
/// shared by every object of the template.

/// \fn Module *ClearanceTestingSlowDeathBehavior::friend_newModuleInstance(Thing *thing, const ModuleData *moduleData)
/// \brief Instance factory registered for
///        "ClearanceTestingSlowDeathBehavior": creates the module for one
///        object.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModule calls it through the registration. The group
/// page describes the shared frame.
///
/// \param thing       The object being built; the module keeps it as its
///                    owner.
/// \param moduleData  The template's
///                    ClearanceTestingSlowDeathBehaviorModuleData.
/// \return The new module as the Module base the factory stores, or null
///         when the allocation fails.
/// \see ClearanceTestingSlowDeathBehaviorModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \fn ModuleData *ClearanceTestingSlowDeathBehaviorModuleData::friend_newModuleData(INI *ini)
/// \brief Data factory registered for "ClearanceTestingSlowDeathBehavior":
///        creates the module data and parses the module's INI block into
///        it.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModuleDataFromINI calls it through the registration.
/// The group page describes the shared frame. The parse step first adds
/// SlowDeathBehaviorModuleData's two tables (the slow-death fields and the
/// death conditions) and then the clearance table.
///
/// \param ini  The reader positioned on the module's block, or null to
///             keep the constructor defaults.
/// \return The new module data as the ModuleData base the factory stores.
/// \see ClearanceTestingSlowDeathBehavior::friend_newModuleInstance


