/// \class GateOpenAndCloseBehavior
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_behavior_module_factories_a
/// \brief Behavior module registered as "GateOpenAndCloseBehavior": a gate
///        configured by open and closed geometries, timings and sounds.
///
/// Its data class reads:
/// - \c OpenByDefault and \c RepelCollidingUnits (booleans);
/// - \c ResetTimeInMilliseconds, \c TimeBeforePlayingOpenSound and
///   \c TimeBeforePlayingClosedSound (durations in milliseconds, stored as
///   logic frames);
/// - \c PercentOpenForPathing, read as an unsigned integer although the
///   name says percent;
/// - \c Proxy (text);
/// - \c GeometryForOpen and \c GeometryForClosed, lists of names read by
///   INI::parseAsciiStringVectorAppend (Zero Hour: that parser appends to
///   the list on every line instead of replacing it);
/// - four sounds: \c SoundOpeningGateLoop, \c SoundFinishedOpeningGate,
///   \c SoundClosingGateLoop and \c SoundFinishedClosingGate.
///
/// Its registration carries the bits Zero Hour uses for the update and
/// collide interfaces. The opening, closing and pathing logic is separate
/// work and is not described here. BFME 1 already has the class.
///
/// \par Instance factory
/// GateOpenAndCloseBehavior::friend_newModuleInstance, the instance factory
/// registered for "GateOpenAndCloseBehavior", has the shared frame
/// described on the group page with one addition. Unlike the other classes
/// in this group, the class's Module base is not at the start of the
/// object, so the factory converts the new pointer to that base, an
/// address inside the allocation, before returning it. The conversion is
/// null-safe: a failed allocation still returns null rather than a small
/// non-null offset.
///
/// \see GateOpenAndCloseBehaviorModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \class GateOpenAndCloseBehaviorModuleData
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_behavior_module_factories_a
/// \brief Module data for GateOpenAndCloseBehavior: the gate's timings,
///        geometries and sounds.
///
/// Built once per module line by
/// GateOpenAndCloseBehaviorModuleData::friend_newModuleData and shared by
/// every object of the template.

/// \fn ModuleData *GateOpenAndCloseBehaviorModuleData::friend_newModuleData(INI *ini)
/// \brief Data factory registered for "GateOpenAndCloseBehavior": creates
///        the module data and parses the module's INI block into it.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModuleDataFromINI calls it through the registration.
/// The group page describes the shared frame.
///
/// \param ini  The reader positioned on the module's block, or null to
///             keep the constructor defaults.
/// \return The new module data as the ModuleData base the factory stores.
/// \see GateOpenAndCloseBehavior


/// \class GettingBuiltBehavior
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_behavior_module_factories_a
/// \brief Behavior module registered as "GettingBuiltBehavior": an update
///        module configured by worker, spawn-timer and rebuild fields.
///
/// Its registered data factory is not documented in this group. The one
/// field table it parses holds \c WorkerName and \c EvilWorkerName (text), \c TestFaction,
/// \c RebuildWhenDead and \c UseSpawnTimerWithoutWorker (booleans),
/// \c SpawnTimer, \c RebuildTimeSeconds and \c DisallowRebuildRange
/// (reals), \c HealWeapon (a weapon), three sounds
/// (\c SelfBuildingLoop, \c SelfRepairFromDamageLoop,
/// \c SelfRepairFromRubbleLoop), four percentages of the build cost
/// (\c PercentOfBuildCostToRebuildPristine, \c ...Damaged,
/// \c ...ReallyDamaged and \c ...Rubble) and \c DisallowRebuildFilter (an
/// object filter). The names suggest a structure that is put up by a
/// worker object and can be rebuilt for a share of its cost; this page
/// does not describe the logic. BFME 1 already has the class.
///
/// \see GettingBuiltBehavior::friend_newModuleInstance

/// \fn Module *GettingBuiltBehavior::friend_newModuleInstance(Thing *thing, const ModuleData *moduleData)
/// \brief Instance factory registered for "GettingBuiltBehavior": creates
///        the module for one object.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModule calls it through the registration. The group
/// page describes the shared frame.
///
/// \param thing       The object being built; the module keeps it as its
///                    owner.
/// \param moduleData  The template's module data for this module line.
/// \return The new module as the Module base the factory stores, or null
///         when the allocation fails.
/// \see GettingBuiltBehavior


/// \class GiantBirdSlowDeathBehavior
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_behavior_module_factories_a
/// \brief Slow-death module registered as "GiantBirdSlowDeathBehavior": a
///        slow death with ground-impact effects and crash avoidance.
///
/// Its data class first takes SlowDeathBehaviorModuleData's two tables,
/// the slow-death fields and the death conditions (\c DeathTypes,
/// \c ExemptStatus, \c RequiredStatus, \c DamageAmountRequired,
/// \c MinKillerAngle, \c MaxKillerAngle; the group page lists both), and
/// then adds \c FXHitGround (an FX list), \c OCLHitGround (an object creation list),
/// \c DelayFromGroundToFinalDeath (a duration), \c CrashAvoidKindOfs
/// (read by a parser not identified here), \c CrashAvoidRadius and
/// \c CrashAvoidStrength (reals) and \c NeedToMaintainFlailingHeight
/// (boolean). The names suggest a flying unit that falls, hits the ground
/// and keeps clear of certain kinds of object while it crashes; this page
/// does not describe the logic. BFME 1
/// already has the class.
///
/// \see GiantBirdSlowDeathBehavior::friend_newModuleInstance,
///      GiantBirdSlowDeathBehaviorModuleData::friend_newModuleData,
///      ClearanceTestingSlowDeathBehavior

/// \class GiantBirdSlowDeathBehaviorModuleData
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_behavior_module_factories_a
/// \brief Module data for GiantBirdSlowDeathBehavior: the slow-death and
///        death-condition fields plus the ground-impact and crash-avoidance
///        fields.
///
/// Built once per module line by
/// GiantBirdSlowDeathBehaviorModuleData::friend_newModuleData and shared by
/// every object of the template.

/// \fn Module *GiantBirdSlowDeathBehavior::friend_newModuleInstance(Thing *thing, const ModuleData *moduleData)
/// \brief Instance factory registered for "GiantBirdSlowDeathBehavior":
///        creates the module for one object.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModule calls it through the registration. The group
/// page describes the shared frame.
///
/// \param thing       The object being built; the module keeps it as its
///                    owner.
/// \param moduleData  The template's GiantBirdSlowDeathBehaviorModuleData.
/// \return The new module as the Module base the factory stores, or null
///         when the allocation fails.
/// \see GiantBirdSlowDeathBehaviorModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \fn ModuleData *GiantBirdSlowDeathBehaviorModuleData::friend_newModuleData(INI *ini)
/// \brief Data factory registered for "GiantBirdSlowDeathBehavior": creates
///        the module data and parses the module's INI block into it.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModuleDataFromINI calls it through the registration.
/// The group page describes the shared frame. The parse step first adds
/// SlowDeathBehaviorModuleData's two tables (the slow-death fields and the
