/// \class DynamicPortalBehaviour
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_behavior_module_factories_a
/// \brief Behavior module registered as "DynamicPortalBehaviour": a portal
///        module configured by model bones, waypoints, links and wall
///        options.
///
/// Its registered data factory is not documented in this group. The parse
/// step first adds the shared upgrade fields that upgrade modules use
/// (\c TriggeredBy, \c ConflictsWith, \c RequiresAllTriggers,
/// \c RequiresAllConflictingTriggers, \c CustomAnimAndDuration and
/// \c Permanent; see \ref grp_w1021_upgrade_module_factories), and its
/// registration includes the bit Zero Hour uses for the upgrade interface,
/// which fits a module that reacts to upgrades. Its own fields are
/// \c BonePrefix and \c NumberOfBones, \c WayPoint and \c Link (read by
/// the class's own parsers), \c WallBoundsMesh, \c GenerateNow,
/// \c AboveWall (an unsigned integer), \c TopAttackPos (a coordinate),
/// \c TopAttackRadius, \c AllowEnemies, \c ActivationDelaySeconds and
/// \c ObjectFilter. The names suggest waypoints placed at model bones and
/// linked into paths, for example across walls; the module's logic is not
/// described here. BFME 1 already has the class.
///
/// \see DynamicPortalBehaviour::friend_newModuleInstance,
///      FakePathfindPortalBehaviour, MineshaftPortalBehaviour

/// \fn Module *DynamicPortalBehaviour::friend_newModuleInstance(Thing *thing, const ModuleData *moduleData)
/// \brief Instance factory registered for "DynamicPortalBehaviour": creates
///        the module for one object.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModule calls it through the registration. The group
/// page describes the shared frame.
///
/// \param thing       The object being built; the module keeps it as its
///                    owner.
/// \param moduleData  The template's module data for this module line.
/// \return The new module as the Module base the factory stores, or null
///         when the allocation fails.
/// \see DynamicPortalBehaviour


/// \class FakePathfindPortalBehaviour
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_behavior_module_factories_a
/// \brief Behavior module registered as "FakePathfindPortalBehaviour": a
///        portal module that, by its name, serves pathfinding.
///
/// Its registered data factory is not documented in this group. It builds
/// its data with the same constructor as MineshaftPortalBehaviour's, and the two
/// parse steps are identical: the shared upgrade fields (see
/// DynamicPortalBehaviour) followed by \c AllowEnemies and
/// \c AllowNonSkirmishAIUnits (booleans). Unlike DynamicPortalBehaviour,
/// its registration does not include the upgrade bit; it has the bits Zero
/// Hour uses for update, die and create. Its logic is not described here.
/// The class is not in Zero Hour, and Open-BFME-1's
